  "lineage": "Repertoire of the Mandinka jali harp-lute of the Gambia, Casamance, Guinea-Bissau and Mali, traced to seventeenth-century Kaabu and codified through the Diabaté, Suso and Konte lineages — 21 strings on a calabash-and-cowhide body tuned to one of four modes (sauta, tomora, hardino, silaba), a repeating bass-and-thumb kumbengo ostinato under improvised treble birimintingo runs, and pieces such as Kelefaba, Alalake and Kaira played solo or in duo at flexible tempo.",
